A||||7||BC-GT||Definitive 3.1 build list (looking for)||||1||
Z||000000||BC-GT||07-30-2001||11:19 PM||||85 GT(auto) is going in next week for a motor rebuild. The crank is gone and the front exhaust manifold is cracked in half. The 3.4 swap is out, hard to find a block and harder to find someone to work on it. Found a machine shop that has built a few 2.8's back in the old days, but are more then happy to do anything I want. These guys are old rodders who build boat motors now(mostly), but were more then willing to sit down and talk with me for over an hour(stressed heavily getting everything balanced![88formula!!!] Not looking for a race or the fastest motor around, just a good performing reasonable priced engine. So far I only have a few definite components and need to let these guys know what to use:<BR>Got about 4 grand to spend on the motor EXCLUDING the headers but including machining costs.<BR>--prices in Canadian funds--<P>Sprint or Cwest headers(not sure, both close to a grand Jet Coated)<BR>crank- 3.1 litre casting #981 ($250 prepped)<BR>Silv-O-lite pistons #1486 ($30x6=$180)<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-30-2001||11:35 PM||||You can buy a rebuilt 3.4L for $1500, with a 3 yr warranty from ATK.  Figure another $1000 for injectors, modified strut mounting bracket, relocating the start bolts..... and you can be driving around in a 200 hp car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BC-GT||07-30-2001||11:42 PM||||And there's a ATK store in Vancouver Canada Where??||||reg||1
Z||000003||00lE||07-31-2001||08:33 AM||||Wow, for $4k you should be able to have one of these delivered to your door:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.paceparts.com/ht43.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paceparts.com/ht43.htm</A> <P>Any GM dealership can provide you one, and you would still have plenty $$ left over for some headers and other fun stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BC-GT||07-31-2001||12:44 PM||||00lE, you may be right, just called the Chevy dealer up the street from me and he said he could get me one for $2600.00 Canadian.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||07-31-2001||02:42 PM||||I was told by the GM dealership that they would not provide any warranty with the 3.4 as it was not designed for the Fiero application. That and the fact that the new starter holes had to be drilled. Keep that in mind if your getting it froim them||||reg||1
Z||000006||BC-GT||07-31-2001||03:06 PM||||This is true about warranty but, for that price it's just above what I would be paying to get a <B>quality</B> rebuild on my 2.8. Even the machine shop said I would be crazy not to do it. They said they may even be able to get it cheaper than that. I gave them the info from Ed Parks site today and they will get back to me soon.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wildcat||07-31-2001||11:40 PM||||We just bought a 3.1L core from a 92-95 Lumina Van which has the steel heads.  $250<BR>Had engine professionally rebuilt locally for $1750 incl pst/gst and it works great and is reliable.  No modifications required, used the 2.8 timing cover,water pump, brackets, balance, clutch flywheel, and oilpan.  With all this it is a direct bolt in, a way more reliable engine than chevy's crappy 2.8's.<BR>Got 30k / 18 months warranty.  This was done in Williams Lake, BC.  Price incl block heater oil and filter.<BR>Tim||||reg||1
